Top Most Tricky Docker Interview Questions 
 If you're preparing for high-scale system design or DevOps roles, these Docker questions will truly test your fundamentals and real-world debugging skills.
 Here are some of the toughest questions engineers face in High-level interviews 👇
1️⃣ How does Docker handle layered file systems internally, and what happens when two layers modify the same file?
 2️⃣ What is the exact difference between Docker pause vs stop vs kill, and when does each one matter in production?
 3️⃣ How does Docker isolate network namespaces, and how do packets actually flow from a container to the host?
 4️⃣ What happens inside Docker when you run a container without specifying a PID namespace?
 5️⃣ Can a running container switch its storage driver (overlay2 → devicemapper) without recreation? Explain the internals.
 6️⃣ How does Docker handle image corruption? What if one of the layers is missing on the host?
 7️⃣ Why does a container sometimes use more memory than the cgroup limit you set?
 8️⃣ How does Docker caching actually work during multi-stage builds?
 9️⃣ What happens behind the scenes when you map a host directory (-v /data:/app/data) and then delete files inside the container?
 🔟 How does Docker handle DNS resolution, and what happens when the host DNS changes while containers are running?
These questions go beyond basics—they check your understanding of container internals, Linux namespaces, cgroups, and real production behavior. Perfect for senior DevOps/SRE interviews.
